# Coding Guidelines: Deployment

<purpose>
Follow these guidelines when programming the final product for deployment
</purpose>


## 4. Deployment & MLOps

### 4.1 Model Serving & Inference

181. **Containerize models using Docker for portability**.

182. **Serve models with FastAPI, Flask, or `torchserve`**.

183. **Use asynchronous endpoints for high-throughput inference**.

184. **Batch predictions to improve latency/throughput tradeoffs**.

185. **Deploy on GPU instances if needed, but monitor utilization**.

186. **Use model versioning and rollback strategies**.

187. **Expose only minimal, necessary APIs—lock down inputs**.

188. **Monitor latency, throughput, and prediction quality in prod**.

189. **Use health checks and timeouts to catch stuck inferences**.

190. **Separate pre/post-processing logic from the core model**.

191. **Use prompt templates and chain-of-thought patterns** for stability.

192. **Cache LLM responses where appropriate** to save cost.

193. **Evaluate output determinism with `temperature=0`** when needed.

194. **Use tools like LangChain or Haystack for orchestration**.

195. **Sanitize and validate LLM inputs/outputs rigorously**.

196. **Log prompts, responses, and errors for review**.

197. **Guard against hallucinations and toxic outputs with filters**.

198. **Use retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) for grounded answers**.

199. **Tokenize and monitor costs—track usage tightly**.

200. **Test edge prompts and stress cases like user adversarial input**.

### 4.2 MLOps Pipelines & Monitoring

231. **Use CI/CD for models just like software**—automate tests and builds.

232. **Track everything**—data, code, parameters, metrics, artifacts.

233. **Use ML experiment tracking tools** (e.g., MLflow, Weights & Biases).

234. **Version models and datasets together**—enable reproducibility.

235. **Separate dev, staging, and production environments**.

236. **Automate retraining pipelines with orchestration tools** (e.g., Airflow, Kubeflow).

237. **Use model registries** to manage versions and promote deployments.

238. **Monitor model performance in production continuously**.

239. **Detect and alert on data drift, concept drift, and skew**.

240. **Roll back models safely** if metrics degrade in production.

241. **Deploy using containers and orchestrators** (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).

242. **Decouple inference APIs from training code**.

243. **Use feature stores** to unify online/offline features.

244. **Test pipelines end-to-end with real data snapshots**.

245. **Design for auditability—log predictions, inputs, metadata**.

246. **Secure model endpoints and restrict access**.

247. **Use shadow deployment or canary releases to test new models**.

248. **Measure latency, throughput, failure rates** for infra health.

249. **Keep humans in the loop for critical decisions**.

250. **Keep infra modular—swap tools/libraries without rewrites**.
